WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.000
Welcome to Kelly Sandrine’s corner of the
internet.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:07.908
If you sell a service and you’re tired of
starting from zero every month, you’re in

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:08.802
the right place.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:15.235
Before Kelly ran a marketing agency in
Kigali, she was freelancing on Fiverr

00:00:15.235 --> 00:00:16.577
alongside a nine-to-five.

00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:22.137
She tried print-on-demand and took on
design, social media, and web projects.

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:24.084
She was working harder than ever.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.673
The work coming in was still unpredictable.

00:00:27.295 --> 00:00:28.948
Maybe you know that feeling.

00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:32.000
You post, send DMs, and try to stay
visible.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.780
Then a project ends and you’re back to
wondering where the next client will come

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.090
from.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.767
Even when someone hires you, it’s hard to
explain what made it happen or how to do it

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:43.075
again.

00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:48.456
Kelly started seeing more consistent leads
and bigger deals when she gave people a

00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:50.489
clear path to working with her.

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:55.368
They needed to recognize their problem in
her content, see how she could help, and

00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:56.947
know what to do next.

00:00:57.087 --> 00:00:59.177
That became the Authority Flywheel.

00:00:59.795 --> 00:01:00.980
Start with Attract.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.572
Make a post about one problem one type of
client already has.

00:01:05.712 --> 00:01:06.769
Then Engage.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:11.280
Give them something useful, like a
checklist, and follow up with a question

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.298
about what’s getting in their way.

00:01:13.438 --> 00:01:16.029
Their answer tells you what support might
fit.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.614
That conversation feeds Convert.

00:01:18.754 --> 00:01:21.537
Offer a clear result, scope, and next step.

00:01:21.677 --> 00:01:23.203
After delivery, Ascend.

00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:25.486
Review what changed with your client.

00:01:25.626 --> 00:01:28.660
If there’s another problem you can help
with, discuss it.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.386
If the work is complete, ask for a referral
or permission to share the lesson.

00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:37.774
That approved story gives your next post
something real to teach.

00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:41.234
The next prospect can see how you work
before reaching out.

00:01:41.374 --> 00:01:43.315
That’s how Ascend feeds Attract.

00:01:43.455 --> 00:01:48.503
The same loop adapts to designers, coaches,
trainers, consultants, and creators.

00:01:48.643 --> 00:01:51.191
The audience and offer are yours to choose.

00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:57.123
The playbook gives you a worked example,
worksheets for your own audience and

00:01:57.123 --> 00:02:00.402
pricing, five follow-up emails, and a
thirty-day plan.

00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:05.987
If you’re ready to build a client pipeline
you can repeat, get the Authority Flywheel

00:02:05.987 --> 00:02:06.713
Playbook below.

